<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The above consolidated unaudited financial results have been reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board at their respective meetings held on August 11, 2023. The statutory auditors of the company carried out ‘Limited Review’.       2. The Group operates in a single segment which is “Generation of power through renewable sources”.       3. The group could not proceed with Phase III power project. The capital advances issued in this regard could not be recovered. These advances are supported by a comfort letter issued by M/s. SVL Limited. The net advances receivable by the group is Rs. 4,000 lakhs. Out of the same, Rs. 3,897 lakhs were recovered till date. Considering the amounts recovered, this arrangement did not result in any further impairment to the group.      4. Considering the stay granted by the Hon’ble Supreme Court of India on the order issued of CERC on reduction of floor price, the Group is confident of favourable decision on the appeal and realization of difference of Rs.500/ REC aggregating to Rs.2,071 lakhs of reveivables.  Nevertheless, for the delay in recovering, provision of Rs. 528 lakhs made.      The above matters have been highlighted as an Emphasis of matter in the Limited Review Report.      5. The Rights Issue Committee of the Board approved the Letter of Offer and other related matters at their meeting held on August 10, 2023.            6. These results includes total income of Rs. NIL, total loss after tax of Rs. NIL for the quarter, in respect of subsidiary viz. Amrit Environmental Technologies Pvt. Ltd (AETPL), whose accounts are not prepared as a going concern.          7. Exceptional Items                                                                                                                                                 (Rs. In lakhs)   Particulars Quarter ended Year ended     30-Jun-23 31-Mar-23 30-Jun-22 31-Mar-23     U